cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use cargofinder in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "cargofinder: candidate cargo discovery and ranking for encapsulin nanocompartments"
authors:
  - family-names: "Erkan"
    given-names: "Abdulbaki"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/XXXX-XXXX-XXXX-XXXX"  # TODO: add your ORCID
version: "0.2.0"
license: "MIT"
repository-code: "https://github.com/abakierkan/cargofinder"
abstract: "A transparent, rule-based tool that ranks genes near encapsulin shell genes as candidate cargo, using synteny, operon structure, known cargo class identity, family-aware targeting signals and recurrence across genomes. It reimplements the genome-mining approach of Andreas & Giessen (2021, doi:10.1038/s41467-021-25071-y) as an installable, deterministic tool with inspectable score components; it makes no claim of methodological novelty."
